# Target C — hostile audit of corrected Type-II nonmatching/interface tradeoff

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Reviewed:** `docs/reports/target_c_typeii_nonmatching_interface_tradeoff_2026-09-12.md` after repair.  
**Disposition:** **PASS after correction; old `0.6676585...` floor REJECTED.**  
**Theorem authority:** unchanged; audit.46 remains canonical.  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

## 1. Regression found

The original report set

\[
a=2\sqrt{\Delta_2}=1.9046256137\ldots
\]

and asserted an unconditional Type-II floor

\[
(q-k)/D\ge a-o(1).
\]

That is the same algebraic overclaim already rejected in the corrected loaded-hull report. Canonical Sections 63, 80, and 85 alone give only

\[
\boxed{
\liminf{q-k\over D}
\ge t_*={2\over5}\left(\pi+\sqrt{\Delta_2}\right)
=1.6375621841815\ldots .
}
\]

The larger `2sqrt(Delta_2)` value is conditional on an additional small-defect hypothesis, for example the separately audited `J_aug=o(D)` branch of the interface/augmented-defect theorem.

**Verdict:** original NT.3 REJECTED; corrected `t_*` input PASS.

## 2. Exact nonmatching identities

Canonical Sections 61 and 63 give

\[
2h-q=x_B+Q+2s_Z,
\]

\[
b+Q=2(q-k),
\qquad x_B=b-q.
\]

Thus

\[
x_B+Q=2(q-k)-q
\]

and

\[
2h-q=2(q-k)-q+2s_Z.
\]

Using only `q/D<=pi` with the corrected `t_*` gives the weak bound

\[
\liminf{2h-q\over D}
\ge2t_*-\pi
=0.1335317147\ldots,
\]

not `0.6676585...`.

**Verdict:** exact identities PASS; original numerical substitution REJECTED.

## 3. Train-end scalar coupling

The finite Section-61 train-end inequality is

\[
h-2\le2x_B+3f+(Q-f)+s_Z.
\]

Since `h=(q-k)+s_Z`, the `s_Z` terms cancel. On normalized subsequential limits,

\[
\boxed{t\le2x+2f+Q.}
\]

Put

\[
s=x+Q=2t-q_*.
\]

Because `0<=f<=Q`,

\[
2x+2f+Q\le2x+3Q\le3(x+Q)=3s.
\]

Hence

\[
\boxed{s\ge t/3.}
\]

Since

\[
{2h-q\over D}=s+2s_Z/D,
\]

the corrected consequence of this particular Type-II scalar system is only

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {2h-q\over D}
\ge t_*/3
=0.5458540613938\ldots .
}
\]

Canonical Section 61 already gives the stronger universal floor `c_*=0.609904...`. Therefore the repaired report makes no new nonmatching-floor improvement.

**Verdict:** PASS; old `0.6676585...` improvement claim REJECTED.

## 4. Surviving exceptional-face information

The same valid scalar inequality gives

\[
2f-Q\ge t-2s.
\]

Thus if `s<t/2`, a positive exceptional-face density is forced:

\[
f\ge(t-2s)/2.
\]

Since `2f-Q<=Q<=s`, feasibility also gives `s>=t/3` directly. At the formal endpoint `s=t/3`, all coarse inequalities saturate, forcing

\[
x=0,
\qquad Q=f=s.
\]

This is the real structural content: minimizing interface/nonmatching currency forces linear bounded nonquadrilateral-face currency. It is not a contradiction.

**Verdict:** PASS.

## 5. Interaction with the interface/augmented-defect theorem

The route-local audited theorem now on `main` gives

\[
(q-k)+J_{aug}\ge2\sqrt{R_4}.
\]

Therefore on the extra subbranch `J_aug=o(D)`, one does recover

\[
\liminf(q-k)/D\ge2\sqrt{\Delta_2}.
\]

The original nonmatching report omitted this needed hypothesis. The corrected report now keeps the conditional high-density branch separate.

## 6. Final disposition

Valid after repair:

- the exact normalized scalar coupling;
- `x+Q>=t/3`;
- exceptional-face forcing near equality; and
- conditional recovery of the `1.9046256...` loaded-density value when `J_aug=o(D)`.

Rejected:

- unconditional `(q-k)/D>=1.9046256...`;
- unconditional `(2h-q)/D>=0.6676585...`; and
- the endpoint boundary-pattern discussion attached to that false floor.

**PASS after correction. C-II remains open.**